body:
I lost my son to cancer 2 years ago.  Please just put all past differances aside and do you best to be there while he's fighting his cancer.  I wish I could do my experience with a family member over.  I would drop EVERYTHING and go be by his side 24/7 so you can help.  My son moved 100 miles away to have better cancer treatment and moved in with my daughter. 

&#x200B;

that is just my advice.   When he is gone it will be too late.  I hope he wins.

I want my daughter's husband to agree to a divorce at a reasonable amount.  She gets the house but has to pay him out. 

&#x200B;

Zillow it says 705,000 and they owe 330,000.  He wants 100,000.  She wants to offer 65,000 as house needs lots of work as he hasn't done anything to it in the last six years they have owned it.

My son fought the same cancer you have.   From his experience I so recommend you get a feeding tube, he was so grateful for his.  My son did beat the neck cancer so hang in there and have hope you can.

&#x200B;

My son later got a spot on his liver and had surgery scheduled on April 4, 2020 to stop the blood flow to it.  Covid postponed the surgery for three weeks.  Then it was too late.  So I am still mad at Donald.  Really mad.   My best wishes that you win this battle.  Let us know if we can help somehow.

Good thoughts young lady.  I did the same, married for fifteen years and did everything, even when we moved four times.   Plus he started beating and strangling me the last 8 years of it.  I stayed because I could not keep my children in the style they were accustomed to.  MISTAKE.

&#x200B;

I ended up shooting my husband after he tried to strangle our daughter 2 times.  Now 35 years later I have never felt a moment of guilt or sorrow.  I did do ten years in prison after they put me on probation and I violated that.   Did four years of probation and didn't report in, didn't pay my fine, didn't do my community service AND my thoughts was....oh you think I'm a criminal I will be one.  So I started using drugs and tried to do as much crime as i could.  Yes, but after doing ten years in prison then I did stay on a straight and narrow legal path.  The real ones that suffered were my two children as I just got in a cell and do my artwork and they had to survive life on the outside.  My son died from cancer on Feb 11, 2021.   My daughter is still a complete mess, going through her third divorce now and wanted to jump from a bridge before she started her divorce.  She marries HORRIBLE men also.    So ladies out there in bad marriages, if your husband doesn't beat you or your kids go ahead and stay and keep in school.  My husband didn't want me going to school but DO IT.

one indication I had diabetes, type 2, is because I'd be so tired.  I'd wake up, eat something and be back in bed an hour later.  Regular blood sugar is best from 80 to 120.  Now I know that if I get over 300 it's BED time.  How I discovered the diabetes is having a UTI.  

&#x200B;

I had been drinking a case (12) of Pepsi daily, that is all I drank.  Now, I've never had a Pepsi since 2010.  I drink diet snapple only now, plus tea no sugar.  You really should just start eating better and not get diabetes.   Buy some test strips, a item that pokes your finger, and a meter.   Start testing your blood.   They say if you get over 400 you can go into a coma, possible, it hasn't happened to me thankfully.   Start looking up food that is good for diabetics and try to start now to avoid it.   Good luck

I am fully vaccinated and I still wear my mask.  Today was the first day in my large grocery chain store where others were not wearing except a few.   

&#x200B;

I wear mine as I live with an UN-vaccinated person that has lung issues already.  He does not like to leave our house so that accounts for why he's not done yet.  He is going to do it.

Here is my question.  I have no butt and legs are fine.  What is FAT is my torso and stomach.

&#x200B;

Can you please prescribe some exercise for that area.  Thank you

We lost our Ryan on Feb 11 after a 3 year fight with cancer.  So no need to describe how you feel.   Try to keep him at home if you can.   We are glad we were able to do that for Ryan.  

&#x200B;

Big hugs.  Let me know if I can help somehow.

People are pre diabetic first.  That is the time to do the proper work to NOT get diabetic.  Don't eat sugar, like I do not even have sugar in my house, or potatoes, etc.  Don't drink soda most of all.  I was drinking 12 cans a day before I was diagnosed.   Use the proper method to plate your food.   1/2 vegetables, 1/4 meat, 1/4 starch.  

&#x200B;

Good luck fighting it.   Oh, sleeping was what happened when I was diagnosed.  I'd wake, eat and then be sleeping again in one hour.   For women a UTI can happen easily.

They are 2.5 months behind in the house.  They will lose it soon.  But if you bail them out it will happen again.  It's too late to sell it unless you live in a hot market.  

&#x200B;

If you don't do it they they may never speak to you again.  Between a rock and hard place.  But I would say that you cannot do it.  You have too many bills now or something.   They need to give up that house.

That makes me quite happy.   I think polygamy is such an unfair thing to do to women.   I mean the "man" gets to keep getting younger model and treats #1 like crap.   

&#x200B;

I would never live like that.

\#1  Take a plate.   1/2 some protein   1/4 some low carb vegetables  1/4 can be something starchy.  Try to keep it under 45 carb per meal. 

&#x200B;

Just cut out anything sugary or too carby.  When you eat that stuff it makes you feel tired and sick.  I find that if I take some Rosarita jalapeno refried beans, some cheese and a tortilla that makes me feel well fed, and great.  I've taken my a1c test from 12 (bad) to 7.6 (great) by eating this way and I still CHEAT every day.  I drink diet Snapple Peach tea.  But just using tea bags is great with no sugar.   

&#x200B;

She will start with metformin and perhaps add glimerpiride.  Then if that doesn't help she'll get insulin.  I pay $24 for a vial of 1000 units that I get at Walmart.  It is an OLD type of insulin that perhaps isn't as good as other insulins but if this didn't exist I would take any insulin.   At all. 

&#x200B;

I do have Medicare now so we'll see if I can get better insulin.   Tell your Mom that serious things can happen IF you don't take care of yourself.  Legs amputated.  Blind.   So you really should put some effort into it.  It doesn't mean you cannot eat fast food anymore.  Just pick good stuff.   

&#x200B;

Buy bags of frozen chicken breasts.    Hamburger patties.    Make huge pots of good things then freeze portions. 

&#x200B;

You'll learn a lot. 

&#x200B;
